WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.516 --> 00:00:03.408
A founder closes the laptop at six.

2
00:00:03.428 --> 00:00:12.951
By morning, three agents have sorted the inbox, drafted two client emails and left a short report, and nothing went out without a yes.

3
00:00:12.973 --> 00:00:17.511
This is The One-Person Company, lesson one: agents as staff.

4
00:00:17.536 --> 00:00:26.567
In this lesson: the three kinds of AI help, what changed in 2026, and the four things every agent you hire needs.

5
00:00:26.595 --> 00:00:29.100
Chat assistants answer when you ask.

6
00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:33.188
Desktop agents work on your files while you watch or step away.

7
00:00:33.208 --> 00:00:35.869
The new group is always-on agents.

8
00:00:35.889 --> 00:00:41.871
They run on their own cloud computer, check your apps on a schedule, and message you first.

9
00:00:41.922 --> 00:00:51.318
Three of them launched in a few months: Grok Bot in August, OpenAI dots in September, and Claude Duet in October 2026.

10
00:00:51.338 --> 00:00:54.531
Tools that capable change the founder's job.

11
00:00:54.551 --> 00:00:57.939
You stop opening apps and start managing staff.

12
00:00:57.959 --> 00:01:03.905
Every agent gets a brief, its own access, an approval rule and a regular review.

13
00:01:03.925 --> 00:01:11.976
And one rule sits over all of it: if a task leaves the business or touches money, a human clicks the final button.

14
00:01:12.019 --> 00:01:15.077
First, let's meet the three kinds of AI help.

